@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+# Phase 3b — live rig rerun: every scenario failed in 0.2s with
+`cmux: Error: not_found: Surface not found for the given surface_id`
+Cause (orchestrator's read): the orchestrator closed the old workers pane/tabs by hand between runs; `agent open` reuses a remembered workers pane or surface that no longer exists and fails instead of recovering. Real users close panes all the time.
+Do: before adding a tab, check the remembered workers pane still exists in this workspace (cmux list-panes / list-pane-surfaces); if not, forget it and create a fresh workers pane. If cmux returns not_found on new-surface anyway, recreate once and retry. A closed or vanished worker surface makes `wait` return a clear state (`closed`, exit 8) instead of a cmux error. Test both with the fake cmux (pane removed between opens; surface removed while waiting). Same constraints and commit grouping; don't run the rig. Reply DONE.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/brief-3c.md b/builds/agent-command/brief-3c.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ae75a4c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/brief-3c.md
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Phase 3c — live rig: 5 of 6 pass; the silent-command case is hidden by the thinking rule
+
+Rig now (orchestrator ran it): long follow-up done 16.1s PASS · permission stuck 5.4s PASS · missing binary no_start 60.6s PASS · question done 7.1s PASS · fresh folder trust stuck 3.6s PASS · silent running turn expected stalled, got timeout 45.3s FAIL.
+The orchestrator changed the rig's sleep scenario: Claude Code blocks a standalone `sleep 600` ("Blocked: standalone sleep 600..."), so it now runs `python3 -c "import time; time.sleep(600)"` (committed with this brief). The command now really runs, but Claude's on-screen running timer keeps advancing while the tool runs, so the phase-3 "advancing indicator = thinking" rule keeps it from ever being called stalled. A hung test at 0% CPU (a real stall cause in the evidence) looks exactly like this.
+
+Do:
+1. Tell thinking from a running command: a tool call is open when the transcript has a tool use with no result yet (Claude: tool_use without matching tool_result; Codex: an exec/custom_tool_call begin without its output; Grok: its tool call record without a result, else screen). While a tool call is open, the advancing indicator does NOT reset the stall clock.
+2. New state `long_command` (exit 9): a tool call has been open longer than `--command-after` seconds (default 600; the rig passes 30), with the command text. Distinct from `stalled` (no tool open, no growth, no advancing indicator).
+3. Rig: the silent scenario expects `long_command` (pass `--command-after 30`), and keep a separate `stalled` check only if you can provoke a true no-progress state reliably; otherwise cover `stalled` in unit tests only and say so.
+4. README: the states table gains long_command.
+Same constraints and commit grouping; don't run the rig. Reply DONE.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/brief-3d.md b/builds/agent-command/brief-3d.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..992ff5e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/brief-3d.md
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+# Phase 3d — live rig 5/6; silent command still `timeout`. Root cause found.
+
+The Claude worker's registry record has `session: "cmux-feed-v1:Y2xhdWRl:MDljZTA3N2ItYzUzNy00MjQ0LTkyZjktYWEyYTJlNGE0Zjgx"` and `transcript: null`. That session value is cmux's encoding: `cmux-feed-v1:<base64 vendor>:<base64 session id>` (here "claude" and "09ce077b-c537-4244-92f9-aa2a2e4a4f81"). agent never decodes it, so it never finds ~/.claude/projects/<encoded cwd>/09ce077b-….jsonl — which DID record the open tool_use at once (tool_use at 23:00:55 while running, tool_result only when killed at 23:01:35). So long_command could not fire.
+Do: decode cmux feed session ids (both parts base64) wherever they are read (Claude, and check Codex/Grok records too — Codex workers resolved their rollout, verify why and whether by luck); resolve the Claude transcript from the decoded id (match by filename across ~/.claude/projects/*/ rather than recomputing the cwd encoding, which also replaces '.' and other characters); add a unit test with this exact encoded value; a worker whose transcript can't be resolved within 30s after its session starts gets reported in `wait --json` as `transcriptMissing: true` so this can never silently disable detection again. Same constraints and grouping; don't run the rig. Reply DONE.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/brief.md b/builds/agent-command/brief.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1ac6ba5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/brief.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+You are the builder for PR 1 of builds/agent-command/plan.md ("the `agent` command") in this repo (Agent Config Studio, Node, no new dependencies). Work only in this worktree, branch agent-command.
+
+OBJECTIVE: ship an `agent` CLI that starts any model family as a watchable worker in a cmux pane and lets an orchestrator (Claude Code or Codex) open, wait on, message, read and close it. Exactly the "PR 1" section of the plan, nothing from PR 2/3 or Later.
+
+READ FIRST:
+- builds/agent-command/plan.md (spec; PR 1 section is your scope)
+- builds/agent-command/prototype/agent.py, done.py, t1.py, t2.py, t4.py: a working Python prototype proven live today. Port its behaviour to Node; do not ship Python.
+- builds/agent-command/fable.out (research: transcript locations per harness)
+- bin/model-id.mjs, bin/pause.mjs and bin/acs (how a CLI here is structured, dispatched and installed; `acs install-model-id` installs model-id + ask-model onto PATH — install `agent` the same way)
+- lib/paths.js (file reads must go through its readers: tests/setup-guards.mjs fails any raw read outside lib/paths.js), lib/roles.js and lib/models.js (vendorOf, family → id)
+- ~/.claude/skills/cmux/SKILL.md (cmux CLI rules: prefixed refs, --json, close-surface --force)
+
+FACTS FROM THE LIVE TESTS (design must keep these):
+- Launch: write a small launcher script per worker that cd's and execs the harness with the prompt read from a file ("$(cat file)"); pass it to `cmux --json --id-format both new-pane|new-surface ... --command <script>`. Never type the prompt into the terminal.
+- Harness flags: gpt-* → `codex -m <id> [-c model_reasoning_effort=<e>] -s workspace-write -a never`; claude-* → `claude --model <id> [--effort <e>] --permission-mode auto`; grok-* → `grok -m <id> --always-approve`.
+- Layout: side-by-side splits fail after ~7 with "no_space"; open workers as tabs (`new-surface --pane <workers pane>`) in one workers pane created on first use beside the orchestrator's pane (from `cmux --json identify` caller.pane_ref, or $CMUX_SURFACE_ID's pane). Grok only starts while its pane is visible+focused: give Grok its own new pane with --focus true, wait until its session dir appears under ~/.grok/sessions/<cwd with / as %2F>/ (≤6s), then `cmux focus-pane --pane <orchestrator pane>`.
+- Done detection (cmux Stop events are dropped for Codex under load; Grok never sends Stop): Codex → `task_complete` lines in ~/.codex/sessions/Y/M/D/rollout-*.jsonl whose first line's payload.cwd matches (track the specific rollout by session id once known); Claude → agent.hook.Stop for the surface in ~/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl (also usable: the session transcript ~/.claude/projects/<cwd with / → ->/<session>.jsonl); Grok → `turn_ended` in ~/.grok/sessions/<enc cwd>/<id>/events.jsonl.
+- Stuck detection: agent.hook.PermissionRequest (and Notification not within ~60s after a finished turn, which is just the idle notice) for that surface_id.
+- Final answer: Codex task_complete.last_agent_message; Claude last assistant text in its transcript; Grok: last assistant message in chat_history.jsonl if present, else the screen (`cmux read-screen`).
+- Follow-ups: `cmux send` + `send-key enter`; one enter sometimes leaves the text in the composer — verify submission from the harness files (a new user turn), retry enter up to 3 times; screen text alone is not a reliable check (the message stays visible in history).
+
+COMMANDS: agent open | wait | send | answer | close | list, as the plan says; `wait` prints done|stuck|timeout (stuck includes the prompt text from read-screen) and exits 0/3/4; JSON output with --json. Registry: one JSON file per worker in ~/.agent-config-studio/agents/ (written with the repo's safe write pattern). close = cmux close-surface --force + status closed; idle close after 30 minutes is checked lazily by `agent list`/`agent wait` (no daemon). Outside cmux (no CMUX_SOCKET_PATH / socket unreachable): plain error "agent needs cmux…", exit 2.
+
+CONSTRAINTS: no new deps; Node ≥ the repo's engines; no personal paths or names in shipped files; comments only where they say why; the frozen file and review gate untouched; no changes outside what PR 1 needs (bin/, lib/ new module(s), README section, acs help + install, tests/SUITE). Test-first. Tests must not need real cmux or real CLIs: inject a fake `cmux` on PATH and fake transcript folders under a temp HOME (look at how tests/pause-cli.mjs and tests/roles-pause.mjs build temp homes and stubs). Never weaken an existing assertion.
+
+VALIDATE: node tests/<your new test files>, node tests/setup-guards.mjs, node tests/guards.mjs, node tests/suite-coverage.mjs, node tests/readme.mjs, node tests/ui-words.mjs (outside the sandbox if it binds a port). Do NOT run a live check that opens real panes — the orchestrator does that.
+
+COMMITS: commit at the end of each phase (core + open/wait; send/answer/close/list; install + README), build folder included. Never push, open a PR or run reviews or other models.
+
+STOP WHEN: all PR 1 requirements have passing tests and the listed suites pass; then write builds/agent-command/report.md (shas, which test covers what, deviations) and reply DONE with a 5-line summary. If the plan doesn't decide something, choose the simplest option, note it in report.md, and continue (don't stop to ask).
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/fable.out b/builds/agent-command/fable.out
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bae7761
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/fable.out
@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+## VERDICT
+
+Don't change how agents run: every vendor already writes a live transcript to disk, so watch those. Start with a cmux pane that tails the transcript, then build one ACS "Agents" board on the same files.
+
+The key fact: all 137 Codex sessions today were headless `codex exec`, and each one wrote a full transcript as it ran (messages, every command with exit code and output, reasoning summaries). They also already emit events to cmux's event bus. Your "headless = unwatchable" rule is a viewer gap, not a data gap.
+
+## OPTIONS
+
+| # | Option | What he sees, where | Step in | Effort | Works here? |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **Watch pane**: keep headless, open a cmux split that tails the transcript through `jq` | One line per step (message, command, exit code), live, in a pane next to the orchestrator | Stop only (kill the process); follow-up via `codex exec resume <thread_id>` after the turn | S | Formatter tested on a finished Codex transcript; live tailing and pane opening not run |
+| 2 | **ACS "Agents" board**: ACS tails the transcript folders of all three vendors and pushes to a page | Every running agent, any vendor, one page: role, model, cwd, last step, expandable transcript | Stop button (kill pid); message via resume | M | Pieces exist: ACS has SSE and already parses Codex and Grok session files for usage. Not built |
+| 3 | **Interactive TUI in a cmux pane** (`codex "<brief>"`, `grok "<brief>"`) instead of headless | The vendor's real UI, live | Full: type into it, interrupt, approve | S–M | Your two skills already cover sending prompts and waiting for `Stop`. Not run |
+| 4 | **cmux Feed** (`cmux right-sidebar feed`, `cmux feed tui`) | Tool calls across Claude and Codex in cmux's sidebar | Feed approvals | Zero | Events are flowing (about 1,000 Codex feed items in the last 20k events); I couldn't open the UI |
+| 5 | **Codex daemon viewer** (`codex agents`, `codex remote-control start/pair`) | Codex's own session browser; pairing code for a remote device | Yes (`codex queue --thread --message`) | M | Daemon is not running, so today's exec runs don't go through it. Codex only, experimental |
+| 6 | **Stream ingest**: launchers tee `--json` / `stream-json` / `streaming-json` into a runs folder ACS watches | Same board as #2 | Same as #2 | S–M on top of #2 | Only needed for Grok (see notes) |
+| 7 | **cmux agent-session surface** (`cmux new-surface --type agent-session --provider codex\|claude\|opencode`) | A native GUI session tab in cmux | Presumably full | S to try | Flag exists; no Grok provider; untested |
+| 8 | **Claude wrapper subagent**: a cheap Claude subagent whose only job is to run `codex exec` and relay | Shows in Claude Code's native subagent UI | Via SendMessage to the wrapper | S | Would work, but output arrives in chunks and the wrapper may paraphrase |
+| 9 | **Phone** | See notes | | | |
+
+Notes:
+
+- **Transcript locations (all checked):**
+  - Codex: `~/.codex/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/rollout-*.jsonl`, local date; the final answer is in `task_complete.last_agent_message`.
+  - Claude: `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session>.jsonl`, with subagents under `<session>/subagents/agent-*.jsonl`.
+  - Grok: `~/.grok/sessions/<cwd>/<id>/`.
+- **Grok is the weak spot.** Its on-disk files are thin: `events.jsonl` is almost all `phase_changed`, and tool calls in `chat_history.jsonl` carry only `kind` and `type`. For Grok, use #6 (`--output-format streaming-json` teed to a file) or #3.
+- **`ask-model` buffers stdout** until exit (`tools/ask-model.mjs:1021`), so it shows nothing live itself. Codex calls through it still write the rollout file, so #1 and #2 cover them without touching it.
+- **#3 loses structured output.** A TUI can't take `--output-schema` or `--json-schema`, so reviewer and grader calls that need a schema should stay headless. It suits builders and the docs writer.
+- **#4 is partly redacted.** The event bus drops tool input; `~/.cmuxterm/workstream.jsonl` keeps it truncated with paths replaced by `<path>`. Good for "is it alive and what tool", not for reading the work.
+- **#5 doesn't see exec runs.** There is no control socket at `~/.codex/app-server-control/`, despite `daemon_auto_start` being on. Using it means launching workers through the daemon (`--remote unix://`), a bigger change than tailing files.
+- **Phone:**
+  - Best route: put the #2 board behind Tailscale (app installed; I couldn't check its status).
+  - ACS blocks this today: it binds to 127.0.0.1 and refuses any non-localhost Host header (`server.js:1783`, `:1915`).
+  - ACS also has write endpoints, so expose a separate read-only board route, not the whole app.
+  - Per-vendor alternatives: `claude --remote-control` for Claude sessions; `codex remote-control pair` for Codex (untested).
+
+## RANKING
+
+1. **Watch pane (#1).** About an hour, no launcher changes, and it removes the constraint for Codex roles today.
+2. **ACS Agents board (#2, plus #6 for Grok).** The "one place, every vendor" answer, and the only one that leads to phone access.
+3. **Interactive pane (#3) for the roles where you want to steer**, such as builders and the docs writer. It is the only option with real mid-turn step-in.
+
+## FIRST PROTOTYPE
+
+The watch pane, on one real Codex run.
+
+1. Start any headless Codex job the way you do now.
+2. In a cmux split, run:
+   ```bash
+   F=$(ls -t ~/.codex/sessions/$(date +%Y/%m/%d)/rollout-*.jsonl | head -1)
+   tail -n +1 -F "$F" | jq -r --unbuffered '
+     select(.type=="event_msg" and .payload.type=="item_completed") | .payload.item |
+     if .type=="CommandExecution" then "$ \(.command[-1]|.[0:200])  → exit \(.exit_code)"
+     elif .type=="AgentMessage" then "\n💬 \(.content|map(.text)|join(""))"
+     else empty end'
+   ```
+3. Once that works by hand, have the orchestrator open it itself with `cmux new-split right --command "<the above>" --focus false` right after launching the worker.
+
+It worked if lines appear while the job is still running, within a second or two of each command, and the final message matches what the orchestrator gets back. I ran this filter's logic against a finished transcript and it printed readable steps; `.command[-1]` and the `.content` join are small tweaks I did not re-run.
+
+One thing to settle in the test: "newest file" picks the wrong run when two Codex jobs start together. The fix is to match on the thread id from `codex exec --json` or on `cwd` in the file's first line.
+
+## RISKS
+
+- **Transcript formats are private and change with CLI updates.** The Codex field names above are from 0.160.0. Keep the parser per-vendor and small.
+- **Experimental surfaces:** the Codex daemon, remote-control, and cmux agent-session are all marked experimental or untested here.
+- **Phone exposure:** anything that opens ACS beyond localhost weakens a deliberate guard. Transcripts contain code and command output.
+- **Interactive panes can stall** on a permission prompt nobody sees. Launch with explicit sandbox and approval flags, and watch for `agent.hook.Notification`.
+- **Not verified:** the sandbox blocked the cmux socket, so no pane or Feed command was run; I could not fetch cmux's Feed docs; no Grok run from today was available to sample.
+
+## QUESTIONS
+
+1. **Is watch-only enough for cross-vendor workers, or do you need to message them mid-turn?** Recommended: watch plus stop is enough for reviewers, advisors and QA; use the interactive pane only for builders and the writer.
+2. **Should the board live in ACS or stay in cmux?** Recommended: ACS. It is the only route to the phone and to a single cross-vendor page; the cmux pane is the stopgap.
+3. **Once the watch pane works, do you want the context-pass rule ("writer must be a native Claude subagent") loosened to allow any vendor?** Recommended: yes, since that rule exists only for watchability. The writer needs write access, which `ask-model` (read-only) can't give, so it would need a `codex exec --sandbox workspace-write` path.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/plan.md b/builds/agent-command/plan.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f090345
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Watchable agents — plan
+
+Decided with Cris 2026-11-13. Research: fable.out (Fable's options). Experiments (scratchpad prototypes agent.py, done.py, t1/t2/t4): every harness runs in a cmux pane with the task passed in at launch; 47 KB prompts work; follow-ups keep context; ten workers at once finish correctly; a sandboxed Codex orchestrator can open a Claude worker; a stuck prompt is caught in ~4s and answered in the pane.
+
+## Problem
+Workers from another vendor (Codex: Sol, Terra, Astra; Grok), and every review, advisor and security pass, run in a hidden shell. Cris can't see what they do, can't step in when one gets stuck, and some roles are forced onto Claude only because Claude subagents are the only watchable kind.
+
+## Rule (goes into the skills and CLAUDE.md lanes)
+| Worker | Runs as |
+|---|---|
+| Claude model, Claude Code orchestrator, building | native subagent (unchanged) |
+| Claude model Cris will want to type to, or a job that should outlive the session | `agent` pane |
+| Codex or Grok, any job | `agent` pane |
+| Review, security, advisor, grade | headless as today (proven model, exact format, read-only, blind), made visible by the sidebar line and the review pane (PR 3) |
+
+## PRs (each stands alone)
+
+### PR 1 — the `agent` command (ACS repo, installed on PATH like model-id)
+- `agent open <family> [--effort e] [--cwd d] [--role r] (--prompt-file f | "<task>")` → prints the worker id. Family → harness through model-id: `gpt-` → `codex -m … -s workspace-write -a never`; `claude-` → `claude --model … --permission-mode auto`; `grok-` → `grok -m … --always-approve`. The prompt never passes through the terminal: a launcher script reads it from a file.
+- Layout: workers open as tabs in one "workers" pane beside the orchestrator (created on first use); Grok gets its own visible pane, focused only until its session starts, then focus returns.
+- `agent wait <id> [--timeout]` returns `done`, `stuck` (with the prompt text from the screen) or `timeout`. Done is read from each harness's own files (Codex `task_complete` in its rollout, Claude transcript / Stop, Grok `turn_ended`); stuck from cmux PermissionRequest/Notification, ignoring the idle notice sent ~60s after a finished turn.
+- `agent send <id> "<text>"` (submit verified from the transcript, not the screen), `agent answer <id>` (final message, exact), `agent close <id>`, `agent list` (this orchestrator's workers).
+- Registry: one file per worker in ~/.agent-config-studio/agents/ (orchestrator workspace and pane, family, model, effort, cwd, surface, session, status, times). Feeds the board later.
+- Closing: a worker closes when the orchestrator accepts its work (`agent close`), or after 30 idle minutes with its transcript kept. Never on its own while it might get a correction.
+- Light on the Mac: workers start with no MCP servers unless the brief asks for one (`--mcp` to opt in), and at most 4 run at once; extra `agent open` calls queue and start as slots free.
+- Not in cmux: a plain message saying the command needs cmux; nothing else in ACS depends on it.
+
+### PR 2 — skills use it (Cris's skills on this Mac, Claude and Codex twins)
+- The rule above in the delegation and /build skills; the orchestrator runs `agent wait` as a background task, so it is notified on done or stuck, answers routine prompts in the pane and brings Cris only real decisions.
+- context-pass: the writer may be any family; a non-Claude writer runs through `agent open` with write access.
+
+### PR 3 — watching judgment agents (review gate: precise lane)
+Covers every headless judgment call, not only reviews: code review, security, Grade, advisor, investigator and second opinions (everything through review.mjs and ask-model).
+- Sidebar line: each running review, security pass, advisor or grade sets a cmux sidebar status for its workspace ("security · fable · reading server.js", "review · sol · 1 finding so far"), cleared when it ends.
+- One review pane: all reviewers of a run stream into a single pane, one line per step, tagged by reviewer; opt-in setting in the review gate (default on for Cris), closes when the run ends.
+- Headless calls stay headless: same model proof, same format, same read-only sandbox.
+
+### Later (separate plan)
+- ACS Agents board — a window, not a control panel: it shows what each agent is thinking, doing and returning; it does not start, route or manage agents (stop is the only action). Every orchestrator workspace, its native and pane workers, and its reviews, live, with transcripts on click (read-only, localhost).
+- Phone access to the board.
+
+## Out of scope
+Changing review independence or the read-only sandbox; a warm pool of idle workers; non-cmux terminals.
+
+## Acceptance
+- PR 1: tests with a fake cmux and fake transcripts for every command; one live check per harness (Codex, Claude, Grok) on a scratch folder: open → done → send → done → answer → close, no prompts reaching Cris; ten at once.
+- PR 2: a real build phase runs a Sol builder in a pane end to end; a docs pass runs on Terra.
+- PR 3: a real /pr-review shows sidebar lines and the review pane; summary and findings unchanged byte for byte against a headless run of the same review.
+
+Lanes: PR 1 standard; PR 2 Cris's config (shown and backed up first); PR 3 precise.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/agent.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/agent.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0b6e2bc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/agent.py
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Prototype `agent open`: start any model family in a cmux pane, prompt from a file of any size.
+Usage: agent.py open <family> <effort|-> <cwd> <prompt-file>   -> prints JSON {surface_ref, surface_id, launched_at}
+       agent.py wait <surface_id> [timeout]                    -> prints when it started, stopped or got stuck"""
+import json, os, shlex, subprocess, sys, time
+env = dict(os.environ, CMUX_QUIET='1')
+EV = os.path.expanduser('~/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl')
+RUN = os.path.join(os.environ.get('TMPDIR', '/tmp'), 'agent-runs')
+
+def harness(family, model, effort):
+    if model.startswith('gpt-'):
+        e = f" -c model_reasoning_effort={effort}" if effort else ''
+        return f"codex -m {model}{e} -s workspace-write -a never"
+    if model.startswith('claude-'):
+        e = f" --effort {effort}" if effort else ''
+        return f"claude --model {model}{e} --permission-mode auto"
+    if model.startswith('grok-'):
+        return f"grok -m {model} --permission-mode auto"
+    sys.exit(f'no harness for {model}')
+
+def open_(family, effort, cwd, pfile):
+    model = subprocess.run(['model-id', family], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip()
+    effort = None if effort == '-' else effort
+    os.makedirs(RUN, exist_ok=True)
+    # The prompt never goes through the terminal: a launcher script reads it from the file.
+    script = os.path.join(RUN, f'{family}-{int(time.time()*1000)}.sh')
+    with open(script, 'w') as f:
+        f.write(f'#!/bin/sh\ncd {shlex.quote(cwd)} || exit 1\nexec {harness(family, model, effort)} "$(cat {shlex.quote(os.path.abspath(pfile))})"\n')
+    os.chmod(script, 0o755)
+    t0 = time.time()
+    grok = model.startswith('grok-')
+    pane = os.environ.get('AGENT_WORKER_PANE')   # set: open as a tab in that pane, which never runs out of room
+    args = (['new-surface', '--pane', pane] if pane else ['new-pane', '--direction', 'right'])
+    out = json.loads(subprocess.run(['cmux', '--json', '--id-format', 'both', *args,
+        '--focus', 'true' if grok else 'false', '--command', script], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env).stdout)
+    if grok:   # grok's TUI waits for focus before it starts: hold it until its session exists, then hand it back
+        me = os.environ.get('AGENT_HOME_PANE')
+        import glob
+        enc = glob.escape(cwd.replace('/', '%2F'))
+        deadline = time.time() + 6
+        while time.time() < deadline:
+            if any(os.path.getmtime(d) >= t0 for d in glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(f'~/.grok/sessions/{enc}/*/'))): break
+            time.sleep(0.1)
+        if me: subprocess.run(['cmux', 'focus-pane', '--pane', me], env=env, capture_output=True)
+    print(json.dumps({'family': family, 'model': model, 'effort': effort, 'surface_ref': out['surface_ref'],
+                      'surface_id': out['surface_id'], 'open_s': round(time.time()-t0, 2), 'launched_at': t0}))
+
+def wait(sid, timeout=600, since=None):
+    t0 = time.time(); start = None
+    with open(EV) as f:
+        f.seek(0, 2) if since is None else None
+        while time.time() - t0 < timeout:
+            line = f.readline()
+            if not line: time.sleep(0.1); continue
+            try: e = json.loads(line)
+            except Exception: continue
+            if (e.get('surface_id') or '').upper() != sid.upper(): continue
+            n = e.get('name', '')
+            if n == 'agent.hook.UserPromptSubmit' and start is None: start = time.time()
+            if n in ('agent.hook.Notification', 'agent.hook.PermissionRequest'): return 'stuck', time.time()
+            if n == 'agent.hook.Stop': return 'done', time.time()
+    return 'timeout', time.time()
+
+def send(ref, msg):
+    """Type a follow-up and make sure it was submitted: a TUI can leave the text sitting in its composer."""
+    subprocess.run(['cmux', 'send', '--surface', ref, msg], env=env, capture_output=True)
+    tail = msg[-25:]
+    for _ in range(4):
+        subprocess.run(['cmux', 'send-key', '--surface', ref, 'enter'], env=env, capture_output=True)
+        time.sleep(1.2)
+        scr = subprocess.run(['cmux', 'read-screen', '--surface', ref], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env).stdout
+        flat = ''.join(scr.split())
+        if ''.join(tail.split()) not in flat[-600:]: return True
+    return False
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    if sys.argv[1] == 'send': print(send(sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3])); sys.exit()
+    if sys.argv[1] == 'open': open_(*sys.argv[2:6])
+    elif sys.argv[1] == 'wait': print(wait(sys.argv[2], float(sys.argv[3]) if len(sys.argv) > 3 else 600))
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/done.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/done.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..58e3c31
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/done.py
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+"""Per-harness 'finished a turn' detection from each CLI's own files, plus 'stuck' from cmux."""
+import glob, json, os, time
+H = os.path.expanduser('~')
+EV = f'{H}/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl'
+
+def codex_turns(cwd, since):
+    n = 0
+    for f in glob.glob(f'{H}/.codex/sessions/*/*/*/rollout-*.jsonl'):
+        if os.path.getmtime(f) < since: continue
+        try:
+            with open(f) as fh:
+                first = json.loads(fh.readline())
+                if (first.get('payload') or {}).get('cwd') != cwd: continue
+                n += sum(1 for l in fh if '"task_complete"' in l)
+        except Exception: pass
+    return n
+
+def grok_turns(cwd, since):
+    n = 0
+    enc = cwd.replace('/', '%2F')
+    for d in glob.glob(f'{H}/.grok/sessions/{glob.escape(enc)}/*/'):
+        f = d + 'events.jsonl'
+        if os.path.exists(f) and os.path.getmtime(f) >= since:
+            n += sum(1 for l in open(f) if '"turn_ended"' in l)
+    return n
+
+def claude_turns(sid, off):
+    n = 0
+    with open(EV) as f:
+        f.seek(off)
+        for l in f:
+            if sid in l and '"agent.hook.Stop"' in l: n += 1
+    return n
+
+def stuck(sid, off):
+    with open(EV) as f:
+        f.seek(off)
+        for l in f:
+            if sid in l and '"agent.hook.PermissionRequest"' in l: return True
+    return False
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/t1.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t1.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..079b2d5
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t1.py
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+"""Test 1: long prompt, then a follow-up in the same pane; does each worker keep its context?"""
+import json, os, subprocess, sys, time
+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(__file__)); import done
+S = os.path.dirname(__file__); T = sys.argv[1]; fams = sys.argv[2:]
+env = dict(os.environ, CMUX_QUIET='1')
+env['AGENT_HOME_PANE'] = json.loads(subprocess.run(['cmux','--json','identify'],capture_output=True,text=True,env=env).stdout)['caller']['pane_ref']
+W = {}
+off = os.path.getsize(done.EV); t0 = time.time()
+for fam in fams:
+    d = f'{T}/w-{fam}'; os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
+    for f in os.listdir(d): os.remove(os.path.join(d, f))
+    o = json.loads(subprocess.run(['python3', f'{S}/agent.py', 'open', fam, '-', d, f'{T}/prompt-{fam}.md'], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env).stdout)
+    W[fam] = dict(d=d, ref=o['surface_ref'], sid=o['surface_id'], model=o['model'])
+def turns(fam, w):
+    m = w['model']
+    if m.startswith('gpt-'): return done.codex_turns(w['d'], t0 - 5)
+    if m.startswith('grok-'): return done.grok_turns(w['d'], t0 - 5)
+    return done.claude_turns(w['sid'], off)
+def wait_turn(k, label):
+    pend = set(W)
+    while pend and time.time() - t0 < 600:
+        for fam in list(pend):
+            if turns(fam, W[fam]) >= k: W[fam][label] = round(time.time() - t0, 1); pend.discard(fam)
+        time.sleep(0.5)
+wait_turn(1, 'turn1')
+t1 = time.time()
+for fam, w in W.items():
+    msg = f'Follow-up, without re-reading any file: from the reference I gave you earlier, what is the text of the FIFTH level-2 heading? Write it as the only line of ANSWER2-{fam}.md, then reply DONE2.'
+    w['sent'] = subprocess.run(['python3', f'{S}/agent.py', 'send', w['ref'], msg], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env).stdout.strip()
+wait_turn(2, 'turn2')
+for fam, w in W.items():
+    a = os.path.join(w['d'], f'ANSWER2-{fam}.md')
+    print(fam, 'sent', w.get('sent'), 'turn1', w.get('turn1'), 'turn2', w.get('turn2'), 'answer2:', open(a).read().strip() if os.path.exists(a) else None, w['ref'])
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/t2.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t2.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3845155
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t2.py
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+"""Test 2: ten workers at once, small task each; all must finish, answers checked, load sampled."""
+import json, os, subprocess, sys, time
+sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(__file__)); import done
+S = os.path.dirname(__file__); T = sys.argv[1]; fams = sys.argv[2:]
+env = dict(os.environ, CMUX_QUIET='1')
+env['AGENT_HOME_PANE'] = json.loads(subprocess.run(['cmux','--json','identify'],capture_output=True,text=True,env=env).stdout)['caller']['pane_ref']
+wp = json.loads(subprocess.run(['cmux','--json','new-pane','--direction','right','--focus','false'],capture_output=True,text=True,env=env).stdout)['pane_ref']
+env['AGENT_WORKER_PANE'] = wp
+W = {}; off = os.path.getsize(done.EV); t0 = time.time()
+for i, fam in enumerate(fams):
+    k = f'{fam}{i}'; d = f'{T}/ten/{k}'; os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
+    for f in os.listdir(d): os.remove(os.path.join(d, f))
+    n = 17 + i
+    open(f'{d}/prompt.md', 'w').write(f'Compute {n} * {n+1}. Write only the number to RESULT.txt in the current folder, then reply DONE.')
+    o = json.loads(subprocess.run(['python3', f'{S}/agent.py', 'open', fam, 'medium' if fam in ('opus','sol','terra') else '-', d, f'{d}/prompt.md'], capture_output=True, text=True, env=env).stdout)
+    W[k] = dict(d=d, ref=o['surface_ref'], sid=o['surface_id'], model=o['model'], want=str(n*(n+1)))
+print(f'opened {len(W)} in {time.time()-t0:.1f}s; load {os.getloadavg()[0]:.1f}')
+def turns(w):
+    m = w['model']
+    if m.startswith('gpt-'): return done.codex_turns(w['d'], t0 - 5)
+    if m.startswith('grok-'): return done.grok_turns(w['d'], t0 - 5)
+    return done.claude_turns(w['sid'], off)
+pend = set(W); peak = 0
+while pend and time.time() - t0 < 600:
+    peak = max(peak, os.getloadavg()[0])
+    for k in list(pend):
+        if turns(W[k]) >= 1: W[k]['t'] = round(time.time()-t0, 1); pend.discard(k)
+    time.sleep(0.5)
+for k, w in W.items():
+    r = os.path.join(w['d'], 'RESULT.txt'); got = open(r).read().strip() if os.path.exists(r) else None
+    print(f"{k:7s} done {w.get('t')}s  result {got}  {'ok' if got == w['want'] else 'WRONG/none'}  {w['ref']}")
+print(f'all done {time.time()-t0:.1f}s; peak load {peak:.1f}; cores {os.cpu_count()}')
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/t4.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t4.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..36c95ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/t4.py
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+import json, os, subprocess, sys, time
+d = sys.argv[1]; S = os.path.dirname(__file__)
+env = dict(os.environ, CMUX_QUIET='1'); EV = os.path.expanduser('~/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl')
+off = os.path.getsize(EV); t0 = time.time()
+script = os.path.join(os.environ.get('TMPDIR','/tmp'), 'stuck.sh')
+open(script,'w').write(f"#!/bin/sh\ncd '{d}'\nexec claude --model claude-opus-5-5 --effort medium --permission-mode default \"$(cat '{d}/prompt.md')\"\n"); os.chmod(script, 0o755)
+o = json.loads(subprocess.run(['cmux','--json','--id-format','both','new-pane','--direction','right','--focus','false','--command',script],capture_output=True,text=True,env=env).stdout)
+sid, ref = o['surface_id'].upper(), o['surface_ref']
+state = 'waiting'
+with open(EV) as f:
+    f.seek(off)
+    while time.time() - t0 < 180:
+        l = f.readline()
+        if not l: time.sleep(0.1); continue
+        try: e = json.loads(l)
+        except Exception: continue
+        if (e.get('surface_id') or '').upper() != sid: continue
+        n = e.get('name','')
+        if n == 'agent.hook.PermissionRequest' and state == 'waiting':
+            print(f'stuck detected at {time.time()-t0:.1f}s; tool={(e.get("payload") or {}).get("tool_name")}')
+            time.sleep(0.5)
+            scr = subprocess.run(['cmux','read-screen','--surface',ref],capture_output=True,text=True,env=env).stdout
+            q = [x.strip() for x in scr.splitlines() if 'date' in x or 'proceed' in x.lower()][:3]
+            print('screen says:', q)
+            subprocess.run(['cmux','send','--surface',ref,'1'],env=env,capture_output=True)
+            print(f'answered "1. Yes" at {time.time()-t0:.1f}s'); state = 'answered'
+        if n == 'agent.hook.Stop' and state == 'answered':
+            print(f'finished at {time.time()-t0:.1f}s'); break
+print('RESULT:', open(f'{d}/RESULT.txt').read().strip() if os.path.exists(f'{d}/RESULT.txt') else None, ref)
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/prototype/wsend.py b/builds/agent-command/prototype/wsend.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b3b57e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/prototype/wsend.py
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Experiment: send a follow-up into a worker pane and block until that surface's next Stop."""
+import json, os, subprocess, sys, time
+ref, uuid, msg = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3]
+ev = os.path.expanduser('~/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl'); env = dict(os.environ, CMUX_QUIET='1')
+size = os.path.getsize(ev); t0 = time.time()
+subprocess.run(['cmux', 'send', '--surface', ref, msg], env=env, capture_output=True)
+subprocess.run(['cmux', 'send-key', '--surface', ref, 'enter'], env=env, capture_output=True)
+submitted = False
+with open(ev) as f:
+    f.seek(size)
+    while time.time() - t0 < 300:
+        line = f.readline()
+        if not line:
+            if not submitted and time.time() - t0 > 1.5:   # text sat in the composer: press enter once more
+                subprocess.run(['cmux', 'send-key', '--surface', ref, 'enter'], env=env, capture_output=True); submitted = True
+                print(f'second enter at {time.time()-t0:.2f}s')
+            time.sleep(0.1); continue
+        try: e = json.loads(line)
+        except Exception: continue
+        if (e.get('surface_id') or '').upper() != uuid.upper(): continue
+        n = e.get('name', '')
+        if n == 'agent.hook.UserPromptSubmit' and not submitted: submitted = True; print(f'submitted: {time.time()-t0:.2f}s')
+        if n == 'agent.hook.Stop': print(f'Stop: {time.time()-t0:.2f}s'); break
