+++ b/builds/agent-command/report.md
@@ -0,0 +1,131 @@
+# Agent command — builder report
+
+DONE with the requested follow-up. The orchestrator committed the initial implementation as `b4001bb`; these follow-up edits are uncommitted for the orchestrator to split and commit. No live worker panes, reviews, model turns, pushes or PRs were started.
+
+- Guard b permits only `spawnSync` with the literal `cmux` in `lib/agent.js`. A separate import-graph assertion prevents the server from reaching that module through static imports, dynamic imports or re-exports; computed imports fail closed. Negative controls reject harness/other binaries, computed executable names, other subprocess functions, and direct/transitive worker imports. No existing assertion was changed.
+- `--mcp` is accepted and recorded. Claude defaults to `--strict-mcp-config`, without `--mcp-config`; opt-in removes that restriction. Grok is unchanged because it has no no-MCP switch. **Codex also retains configured MCP servers: no global run-only disable key was verified.** README documents both exceptions.
+- Codex launchers resolve `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` after changing cwd and add the physical common directory with `--add-dir` when it is outside cwd. The launcher tests use real temporary Git metadata, including a linked worktree path containing spaces and an apostrophe, plus an ordinary repository that must receive no extra directory.
+
+## MCP verification
+
+`codex --help` documents generic `-c` overrides but no global MCP-off option. The installed CLI is 0.160.0; its installed README contains no such setting. The version-matched [configuration schema](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.160.0/codex-rs/core/config.schema.json) and [config implementation](https://github.com/openai/codex/blob/rust-v0.160.0/codex-rs/core/src/config/mod.rs) were downloaded to temporary files and inspected. `orchestrator.mcp.enabled` concerns orchestrator-owned tools, not all configured servers.
+
+A read-only CLI probe used a temporary HOME with one fixture server; `codex mcp list --json` does not start a model turn:
+
+| Override | Fixture server enabled |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-c mcp_servers={}` | true |
+| `-c orchestrator.mcp.enabled=false` | true |
+| `-c mcp_servers.fixture.enabled=false` | false |
+
+No ineffective global override was added. Per-server enumeration/config rewriting is outside this follow-up.
+
+## Validation
+
+| Command | Result |
+| --- | --- |
+| `node tests/agent-cli.mjs` | PASS, including all harness launcher argv, MCP opt-in/default, shared Git metadata, all commands and queue coverage |
+| `node tests/agent-install.mjs` | PASS, including installed open/wait lifecycle |
+| `node tests/guards.mjs` | 11 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node tests/setup-guards.mjs` | 54 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node tests/suite-coverage.mjs` | 33 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node tests/readme.mjs` | 53 passed, 0 failed |
+| `git diff --check` | PASS |
+
+## Commit grouping
+
+- Guard-only test commit: `tests/guards.mjs`, `tests/setup-guards.mjs`. Existing assertions are intact; additions pin the cmux exception and server isolation.
+- Launcher assertion test commit: `tests/agent-cli.mjs`. Assertions are appended; none are weakened.
+- Implementation/documentation commit: `bin/agent.mjs`, `lib/agent.js`, `README.md`, this report.
+
+Live pane acceptance remains with the orchestrator, as requested. The frozen review test and review-gate files are untouched.
+
+## Phase 2
+
+DONE. Reliability changes are uncommitted, grouped below for the orchestrator. No live panes or fault-rig scenarios were run, and the existing guards were not edited.
+
+- `wait` exposes `state` alongside the compatible `status`: done/0, stuck/3, timeout/4, unsent/5, no_start/6, stalled/7. It recognizes final `QUESTION:` lines, retains exact question-answer text, watches the 10-second submission and 60-second startup deadlines, and checks transcript growth with a default 300-second stall threshold. Stalled diagnostics retain up to three available steps (up to 2,000 characters each), including Grok chat-history tools.
+- `send` requires Codex `task_started`, Claude user text, or Grok `turn_started`; a Codex user-message record alone does not prove submission. Four Enter presses are the maximum, followed by a failure at 10 seconds if no start is confirmed. The pending attempt persists so a separate waiter wakes with unsent. Messages over 400 characters are atomically saved in the worker run directory and replaced with a short file instruction in the composer.
+- Launchers write `harness.pid` before exec and start exactly one `caffeinate -i -w <pid>` per process. Caffeinate output is retained in the run directory; its assertion ends with the target process. README states that a closed lid on battery still sleeps. Interactive stdin is preserved. No non-interactive Codex calls were introduced; the sole Node subprocess (cmux) explicitly ignores stdin.
+- `builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs` creates a scratch Git repo, checks long follow-up/done, permission/stuck, silent sleep/stalled, missing binary/no_start and QUESTION/done. It prints a results table and closes its workers in finally, including orphan records from interrupted opens. Extra harness args and binary replacement require the explicit test-only `AGENT_TEST_MODE=1` gate. The rig was syntax-checked only; live timing acceptance remains with the orchestrator.
+
+### Coverage and checks
+
+| Check | Result / coverage |
+| --- | --- |
+| `node tests/agent-reliability.mjs` | PASS: fake-clock boundaries, background wait waking at startup deadline, all fault states and exit codes, oldest overdue signal, growth resets, default stall threshold, last-three-step diagnostics, all-vendor question detection, Grok screen/history fallbacks, task-start proof and short/long sends |
+| `node tests/agent-cli.mjs` | PASS: all Phase 1 assertions retained; fake transcript starts added; actual launcher execution against fake caffeinate verifies one assertion per recorded harness PID; test-only launch overrides and ignored overrides without the gate |
+| `node tests/agent-install.mjs` | PASS: installed CLI open/wait lifecycle and existing install/refusal checks |
+| `node tests/guards.mjs` | 11 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node tests/setup-guards.mjs` | 54 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node tests/suite-coverage.mjs` | 33 passed, 0 failed; new reliability test is in the offline suite |
+| `node tests/readme.mjs` | 53 passed, 0 failed |
+| `node --check builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs` | PASS; the rig itself was not run |
+| `git diff --check` | PASS |
+
+### Choices and commit grouping
+
+- Exit codes 5/6/7 cover the three new failure states; send failure retains its Phase 1 exit code 1. `--stall-after 0` checks a running turn immediately. Runtime clock/sleep injection is a library test seam; CLI time is real.
+- Unsent includes a best-effort composer line plus the full screen, since terminal output does not provide a structured input-box boundary. Transcript signals, not this screen heuristic, determine submission.
+- No daemon was added. Caffeinate is tied to the launcher/harness PID rather than the short-lived `agent open` process. The prior MCP limitations remain unchanged.
+- Test-only commit group: `tests/agent-reliability.mjs`, additions to `tests/agent-cli.mjs`, `tests/fixtures/agent-cmux.mjs`, `tests/SUITE`, and the fault rig. Existing assertions are unchanged.
+- Implementation/docs group: `lib/agent.js`, `bin/agent.mjs`, `README.md`, this report.
+- **The rig is ignored by the repository's `builds/` rule. Include it explicitly with `git add -f builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs` when committing.** No `.gitignore` or review-gate changes were made.
+
+## Phase 3 — trust dialogs and thinking indicators
+
+Base: `60cfb79` (brief), following implementation `25334ab` and tests `23fb6f0`.
+Changes remain uncommitted for the orchestrator, as instructed.
+
+- `wait` reads pre-session screens every three seconds and returns `stuck`, exit 3, `kind: "trust"`, with ANSI-free dialog lines. Header and choice text must both match. Visible trust takes precedence over `no_start`; a session start invalidates the cached startup dialog. No trust responses or CLI configuration writes were introduced.
+- Bundled text was checked locally in Codex 0.160.0, Claude Code 2.1.325 and Grok 1.0.77. The per-harness fixtures record their exact trust strings; their README distinguishes reconstructed running-status examples from live captures. Grok's full dialog says “Do you trust the contents of this directory?”, with “Yes, proceed” / “No, quit”.
+- Elapsed running indicators are sampled every three seconds and refreshed before a stall decision. The worker record persists the turn, elapsed seconds and last advance time across invocations. Transcript growth or advancing elapsed time resets the stall deadline. Frozen/disappearing indicators and timer resets do not extend it. Choice where unspecified: the first elapsed reading gets one observation window before it can be called frozen.
+- Permission-timeout evidence: the installed cmux Claude wrapper's standard hook settings wire `PermissionRequest` directly to `hooks feed --source claude` (lines 2056 and 2172), independently of the queued `SessionStart` hook. There is no session prerequisite in that wiring. This supports the orchestrator's confirmed cause: folder trust blocks startup before Claude reaches a tool permission request. Offline coverage verifies both pre-session trust and the post-start PermissionRequest path. Live timing after inherited trust still belongs to the orchestrator's rerun.
+- The rig creates a detached worktree of this repository under TMPDIR, runs the existing five scenarios there, and removes it after closing workers. Its sixth scenario initializes a separate new repository and requires `stuck` with `kind: "trust"` within 15 seconds. The permission scenario explicitly rejects trust as a substitute for its tool prompt. Cleanup retains the scratch path and fails if workers cannot close or worktree removal fails. The rig was not executed.
+
+Validation: `node tests/agent-screens.mjs` passes fake-clock dialog latency for all three harnesses, CLI exit 3, no typing, startup-deadline precedence, session-start cache invalidation, post-start permission, persistent/continuous advancing timers beyond two stall windows, frozen/disappearing indicators, minute formatting and reset rejection. `node tests/agent-reliability.mjs`, `node tests/agent-cli.mjs`, `node tests/agent-install.mjs`, `node tests/guards.mjs` (11), `node tests/setup-guards.mjs` (54), `node tests/suite-coverage.mjs` (33), and `node tests/readme.mjs` (53) pass. Rig syntax and `git diff --check` pass.
+
+Commit-ready groups: tests/fixtures/SUITE plus the development rig; separately `lib/agent.js`, README and this report. Existing assertions, guard files, the frozen review test and review gate are untouched. No new dependencies, live panes, reviews or other models. No scope deviations beyond the documented initial-indicator observation window.
+
+## Phase 3b — manually removed panes and surfaces
+
+Base `b0eda8c`; Phase 3 implementation `ad36dc4`, tests `7c71004`. Changes remain uncommitted for the orchestrator.
+
+- Shared-pane reuse checks `list-pane-surfaces` with explicit workspace and pane refs, using the most recent eligible worker. A missing pane is discarded. A `not_found` race during `new-surface` gets exactly one fresh `new-pane --command` attempt; other errors propagate.
+- `wait` probes the surface on every poll, including completed workers whose transcripts remain. Missing surfaces, explicit closures and idle closures return `state`/`status: "closed"`, `closed: true`, exit 8. Detected disappearance persists in the registry. Closing a manually removed surface is idempotent.
+- `tests/agent-surfaces.mjs` first reproduced the failed second open, then passed: pane removed between opens, valid-pane reuse, workspace-scoped validation, creation race recovery, bounded failed recovery, unrelated creation/screen/socket errors, vanished completed surface, disappearance during a running wait, repeated wait, explicit close, manual removal followed by close, and idle-close exit 8.
+- Existing assertion change: `tests/agent-cli.mjs`'s idle-wait assertion still requires `closed: true`; it now parses the exit-8 result directly instead of the exit-0 JSON helper, and additionally requires state `closed` and exit 8. No assertion was loosened. Suggested test commit message: “Test: preserve idle closed:true, require closed state and exit 8; cover removed panes and surfaces”.
+
+Validation passed: `agent-surfaces`, `agent-cli`, `agent-install`, `agent-reliability`, `agent-screens`, `guards` (11), `setup-guards` (54), `suite-coverage` (33), `readme` (53), rig syntax, and `git diff --check`. All named tests run as `node tests/<name>.mjs`. The rig was not run; no real panes were opened.
+
+Commit groups: test-only (`tests/agent-surfaces.mjs`, `tests/agent-cli.mjs`, `tests/fixtures/agent-cmux.mjs`, `tests/SUITE`); implementation/docs (`lib/agent.js`, `bin/agent.mjs`, README, this report). Guards, frozen tests and review gate untouched; no dependencies or scope deviations.
+
+## Phase 3c — open tools use a command deadline
+
+Base `6274ed0`; Phase 3b implementation `d25d3f8`, tests `24db042`. Changes remain uncommitted for the orchestrator.
+
+- `wait --command-after <seconds>` defaults to 600 and reports `long_command`, exit 9, with `command` in JSON and plain output. An unfinished tool prevents `stalled`; an advancing UI timer does not extend its command deadline. `stalled` applies only when no tool is open, no transcript grows and no thinking indicator advances.
+- Calls/results are paired by id: Claude `tool_use`/`tool_result`; Codex function/custom calls and outputs plus exec begin/end events; Grok `assistant.tool_calls`/`tool_result.tool_call_id`, direct tool records and terminal call updates. Local Grok records confirmed the assistant-array and result-id shape (only schema keys/types were inspected). Parallel calls retain individual ages; failed results close calls too. Turn boundaries discard previous calls.
+- Tool ages persist across waits. Transcript timestamps establish age when available; undated calls use their first observation. Records without ids are tracked by transcript position, and unidentified results close the oldest unidentified call. Grok falls back to explicit `Running:`/`Executing:` command rows only when structured call records are unavailable. Grok history growth also counts as transcript activity.
+- The rig's existing silent Python command now expects `long_command` with `--command-after 30`. No live `stalled` scenario was added: a quiet turn without an open tool is not reliably provoked by this rig. True stalls remain covered offline. The rig was syntax-checked, not run.
+
+`tests/agent-commands.mjs` first failed on the missing long-command state and now passes all three vendors, threshold boundaries/default 600, advancing timers during open tools, persistent undated ages, unrelated transcript growth, mismatched/error results, parallel ages, unidentified calls/results, Codex custom/exec records, Grok screen fallback, post-result true stalls, JSON/plain exit 9 and invalid options. Existing reliability assertions are unchanged: their stall fixtures now include matching tool results, preserving last-three-command diagnostics and true-stall checks with no tool left open. New tests separately require unfinished calls, including calls without ids, to use the command deadline.
+
+Validation passed: `node tests/agent-commands.mjs`, `node tests/agent-reliability.mjs`, `node tests/agent-screens.mjs`, `node tests/agent-surfaces.mjs`, `node tests/agent-cli.mjs`, `node tests/agent-install.mjs`, `node tests/guards.mjs` (11), `node tests/setup-guards.mjs` (54), `node tests/suite-coverage.mjs` (33), `node tests/readme.mjs` (53), rig syntax and `git diff --check`.
+
+Commit groups: tests only (`tests/agent-commands.mjs`, fixture updates in `tests/agent-reliability.mjs`, `tests/SUITE`, rig); implementation/docs (`lib/agent.js`, `bin/agent.mjs`, README, this report). Suggested test commit: “Test: separate unfinished command deadlines from stalls after matched tool results”. No assertion was weakened; guards, frozen tests and review gate are untouched. No dependencies, live panes, reviews or other models. Choices where unspecified are recorded above.
+
+## Phase 3d — decode feed sessions and expose missing transcripts
+
+Base `c1da8b0`; Phase 3c implementation `c77122b`, tests `f63dfb7`. Changes remain uncommitted for the orchestrator.
+
+- Session ids normalize from `cmux-feed-v1:<base64 vendor>:<base64 id>` at hook ingestion, registry reads (including already pinned records), and Codex metadata matching. Both components are decoded; malformed encodings and foreign vendors cannot pin a worker. Plain harness ids remain valid.
+- Claude resolves the session filename across the direct project directories under `.claude/projects`, without reconstructing project-directory encoding. When no session id is known, fallback discovery still requires transcript cwd evidence, baseline exclusion and an unambiguous match. Claimed files remain excluded.
+- A known session whose transcript remains unresolved for 30 seconds adds `transcriptMissing: true` to returned wait JSON, including timeout and hook-derived completion. Hook timestamps establish session start; absent/invalid timestamps use persistent first observation. The flag clears once the file resolves. This is an annotation, with no new exit state or shortened wait deadline.
+- Why Codex appeared healthy: prior discovery returned immediately once a transcript was pinned. With no hook yet, a unique cwd match pinned the raw rollout id. An encoded hook arriving first instead blocked raw-id matching. Read-only inspection of recent real rig records found six pinned Codex workers with raw registry ids matching rollout metadata, despite encoded SessionStart hooks. Their prior success therefore depended on discovery order. Available encoded hook vendor components decode to `codex` and `claude`, matching the normalization. No real Grok worker registry records were present; its encoded hook path is covered offline. Inspection printed only aggregate forms/counts, not paths, ids, prompts or answers.
+
+`tests/agent-sessions.mjs` first reproduced the exact live encoded Claude value failing to expose its open tool; it now resolves that filename and returns long_command. It also covers encoded Codex/Grok hooks, nested hook payloads, both Codex arrival orders, saved and already pinned encoded registry records, punctuation in cwd with a differently named Claude project directory, malformed/foreign encodings, all-vendor 29.999s/30s boundaries, late recovery, timestamp fallback, hook-derived done diagnostics and actual CLI timeout JSON. Existing assertions are untouched.
+
+Validation passed: `node tests/agent-sessions.mjs`, `node tests/agent-cli.mjs`, `node tests/agent-install.mjs`, `node tests/agent-reliability.mjs`, `node tests/agent-commands.mjs`, `node tests/agent-screens.mjs`, `node tests/agent-surfaces.mjs`, `node tests/guards.mjs` (11), `node tests/setup-guards.mjs` (54), `node tests/suite-coverage.mjs` (33), `node tests/readme.mjs` (53), rig syntax and `git diff --check`. The rig was not run; no panes were opened.
+
+Commit groups: tests only (`tests/agent-sessions.mjs`, `tests/SUITE`); implementation/docs (`lib/agent.js`, README, this report). Guards, frozen tests and review gate are untouched. No dependencies, reviews or other models. Conservative timing fallback and unchanged wait deadlines are the choices where the brief did not specify behavior.
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs b/builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7701c0b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/rig/run.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,128 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env node
+import fs from 'node:fs';
+import os from 'node:os';
+import path from 'node:path';
+import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
+
+if (!process.env.CMUX_SOCKET_PATH) throw new Error('Run this rig inside cmux with agent installed on PATH.');
+const repo = fs.realpathSync(fileURLToPath(new URL('../../../', import.meta.url)));
+const temp = fs.realpathSync(fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(process.env.TMPDIR || os.tmpdir(), 'agent-fault-rig-')));
+const scratch = path.join(temp, 'worktree');
+let worktreeAdded = false;
+const owned = new Set();
+const rows = [];
+let activeChild = null;
+let interrupted = false;
+for (const signal of ['SIGINT', 'SIGTERM']) process.on(signal, () => { interrupted = true; activeChild?.kill('SIGTERM'); });
+const baseEnv = { ...process.env, AGENT_TEST_MODE: '1' };
+delete baseEnv.AGENT_TEST_BINARY;
+delete baseEnv.AGENT_TEST_LAUNCH_EXTRA;
+function command(binary, args, { env = baseEnv, timeout = 90000, cwd = repo, cleanup = false } = {}) {
+  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
+    if (interrupted && !cleanup && !(binary === 'agent' && ['close', 'list'].includes(args[0]))) return reject(new Error('rig interrupted'));
+    const child = spawn(binary, args, { env, cwd, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] });
+    activeChild = child;
+    let out = '', err = '';
+    child.stdout.on('data', b => out += b);
+    child.stderr.on('data', b => err += b);
+    const timer = setTimeout(() => { child.kill('SIGKILL'); }, timeout);
+    child.on('error', e => { clearTimeout(timer); reject(e); });
+    child.on('close', (code, signal) => { activeChild = null; clearTimeout(timer); resolve({ code, signal, out, err }); });
+  });
+}
+async function open(family, folder, task, env = baseEnv) {
+  const cwd = path.isAbsolute(folder) ? folder : path.join(scratch, folder);
+  fs.mkdirSync(cwd, { recursive: true });
+  const r = await command('agent', ['open', family, '--cwd', cwd, task, '--json'], { env });
+  if (r.code !== 0) throw new Error(r.err || `open failed: ${r.signal}`);
+  const w = JSON.parse(r.out);
+  owned.add(w.id);
+  return w;
+}
+async function wait(w, seconds, extra = []) {
+  const r = await command('agent', ['wait', w.id, '--timeout', String(seconds), '--json', ...extra], { timeout: (seconds + 5) * 1000 });
+  if (!r.out.trim()) throw new Error(r.err || `wait failed: ${r.signal}`);
+  return JSON.parse(r.out);
+}
+async function close(w) {
+  if (!w) return;
+  const r = await command('agent', ['close', w.id], { timeout: 15000 });
+  if (r.code !== 0) throw new Error(`close ${w.id}: ${r.err || r.signal}`);
+  owned.delete(w.id);
+}
+async function scenario(name, harness, expected, limit, body) {
+  const started = Date.now();
+  let w, got = 'error', pass = false, seconds = 0;
+  try {
+    const result = await body(worker => { w = worker; });
+    got = result.state;
+    seconds = (Date.now() - started) / 1000;
+    pass = got === expected && (limit === null || seconds <= limit) && (name !== 'question' || result.question === true) && (name !== 'fresh folder trust' || result.kind === 'trust') && (name !== 'permission' || result.kind !== 'trust');
+  } catch (e) { got = e.message; seconds = (Date.now() - started) / 1000; }
+  finally {
+    try { await close(w); } catch (e) { got += `; ${e.message}`; pass = false; }
+  }
+  rows.push({ scenario: name, harness, expected, got, seconds: seconds.toFixed(1), result: pass ? 'PASS' : 'FAIL' });
+}
+try {
+  const git = await command('git', ['worktree', 'add', '--detach', scratch, 'HEAD']);
+  if (git.code !== 0) throw new Error(git.err);
+  worktreeAdded = true;
+  await scenario('long follow-up', 'codex', 'done', null, async set => {
+    const w = await open('sol', 'long', 'Reply READY as your only answer.'); set(w);
+    const first = await wait(w, 120);
+    if (first.state !== 'done') return first;
+    const message = `${'Reference context. '.repeat(100)}\nReply LONG_OK as your only answer.`;
+    const sent = await command('agent', ['send', w.id, message, '--json'], { timeout: 20000 });
+    const result = await wait(w, 120);
+    if (sent.code !== 0 && result.state === 'done') throw new Error(`send failed without a reported unsent state: ${sent.err}`);
+    const answer = await command('agent', ['answer', w.id]);
+    if (result.state === 'done' && answer.out.trim() !== 'LONG_OK') throw new Error('done with an unexpected long-message answer');
+    return result;
+  });
+  await scenario('permission', 'claude', 'stuck', 15, async set => {
+    const env = { ...baseEnv, AGENT_TEST_LAUNCH_EXTRA: JSON.stringify(['--permission-mode', 'default', '--settings', JSON.stringify({ permissions: { ask: ['Bash'] } })]) };
+    const w = await open('opus', 'permission', 'Use the Bash tool to execute: printf rig_permission_check. Do not answer without executing it.', env); set(w);
+    return wait(w, 15);
+  });
+  await scenario('silent running turn', 'claude', 'long_command', 45, async set => {
+    const env = { ...baseEnv, AGENT_TEST_LAUNCH_EXTRA: JSON.stringify(['--permission-mode', 'auto', '--append-system-prompt', 'This is a fault rig. Execute the requested sleep synchronously with run_in_background=false and wait for its result.']) };
+    const w = await open('opus', 'sleep', 'Use the Bash tool to run python3 -c "import time; time.sleep(600)" synchronously with a timeout of 600000 milliseconds. Do not run it in the background and do not cancel it. Wait for it to finish.', env); set(w);
+    return wait(w, 45, ['--command-after', '30']);
+  });
+  await scenario('missing binary', 'codex', 'no_start', 75, async set => {
+    const w = await open('sol', 'missing', 'This must never run.', { ...baseEnv, AGENT_TEST_BINARY: path.join(scratch, 'missing-harness') }); set(w);
+    return wait(w, 75);
+  });
+  await scenario('question', 'codex', 'done', null, async set => {
+    const w = await open('sol', 'question', 'Reply with this exact single line, without Markdown or additional text: QUESTION: Should I continue?'); set(w);
+    return wait(w, 120);
+  });
+  await scenario('fresh folder trust', 'codex', 'stuck', 15, async set => {
+    const folder = path.join(temp, 'untrusted');
+    const git = await command('git', ['init', folder]);
+    if (git.code !== 0) throw new Error(git.err);
+    const w = await open('sol', folder, 'Reply READY as your only answer.'); set(w);
+    return wait(w, 15);
+  });
+} finally {
+  try {
+    const listed = await command('agent', ['list', '--json'], { timeout: 15000 });
+    if (listed.code === 0) for (const w of JSON.parse(listed.out)) {
+      if (w.status !== 'closed' && w.cwd.startsWith(temp + path.sep)) owned.add(w.id);
+    }
+  } catch (e) { console.error(`Could not check for orphaned rig workers: ${e.message}`); process.exitCode = 1; }
+  for (const id of [...owned]) {
+    try { await close({ id }); } catch (e) { console.error(e.message); process.exitCode = 1; }
+  }
+  console.table(rows);
+  if (worktreeAdded && owned.size === 0) {
+    const removed = await command('git', ['worktree', 'remove', '--force', scratch], { cleanup: true });
+    if (removed.code !== 0) { console.error(`Could not remove rig worktree ${scratch}: ${removed.err}`); process.exitCode = 1; }
+    else worktreeAdded = false;
+  }
+  if (!worktreeAdded && owned.size === 0) fs.rmSync(temp, { recursive: true, force: true });
+  console.log(worktreeAdded || owned.size ? `Scratch retained for cleanup: ${temp}` : 'Scratch worktree removed; harness transcripts remain in the CLI session folders.');
+  if (rows.length !== 6 || rows.some(r => r.result !== 'PASS')) process.exitCode = 1;
+}
diff --git a/builds/agent-command/stalls-summary.md b/builds/agent-command/stalls-summary.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3a742fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/builds/agent-command/stalls-summary.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Why delegated agents stall: summary (Nov 7–15, 2026)
+
+Scope: 6 orchestrator sessions (MAIN = ACS/review gate, GARMAN = Docket/Firstcall/Ledgerline/Askwell, CI, AIRFLO ×2, PERSONAL), 318 MAIN subagent transcripts plus the subagent folders of the other sessions, 1,925 `claude -p` sessions, 717 Codex rollouts, 980 review-log lines, 16 field reports, the task outputs, and the macOS power log (`pmset -g log`). One row per incident, with file:line evidence, is in `incidents.md`.
+
+**Headline:** about **20 hours** of visible stall time in 8 days, plus about 45 hours of wall-clock delay while the Mac slept. Of the 20 incidents with a cost, **the user had to prod in 15**. The orchestrator caught one on its own (E5), and three were never flagged (A2, E1, E4). The single biggest cause is one harness behaviour: **a native subagent's background job finishes, the completion notice goes to the orchestrator's queue instead of the subagent, and the subagent sleeps forever.**
+
+## 1. Causes ranked
+
+| Rank | Cause | Incidents | Time lost (user present) | Who noticed |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | **A. Subagent waits on its own background job or Monitor; the completion never wakes it** | 8 (+1 near miss) | **~14.0 h** (51 + 21 + 23 + 100 + 222 + 400 + 20 min; A2's 2 h 16 min idle not counted) | User prodded 6 of 8; never flagged 1 |
+| 2 | **B. `codex exec` started in the background without `</dev/null`** hangs on stdin | 2 | **~3.5 h** (141 + ~70 min) | User prodded 2 of 2 |
+| 3 | **C. Test command inside `review.mjs --close` hung** (Docket pytest at 0 % CPU) | 2 | **~1.75 h** (25 + 80 min) | User prodded 2 of 2 |
+| 4 | **D. Detached `( … ) &` launch, so no completion notice** | 1 confirmed (C2 was also detached) | **~1 h** | User prodded |
+| 5 | **F. Pane message pasted but not submitted** | 1 | 5 min | User prodded |
+| 6 | **G. Pane worker on a permission prompt** | 1 | 1 min | User |
+| 7 | **H. Fast crashes** (process dies at launch; `cmux: argument too large` for Claude reviewers) | 2 + ~20 | <2 min + unmeasured re-runs | Orchestrator |
+| — | **E. Mac slept with work in flight** (Idle Sleep 3×, Clamshell 2×) | 5 windows, ~15 runs | **~45 h wall clock**, user away | User on return 2, orchestrator 1, nobody 2 |
+
+By count, A leads (8) and E is next (5 windows). By time while the user was present, A alone accounts for about 70 %.
+
+## 2. Earliest automatic signal for each cause, and the recovery that worked
+
+**A. Subagent never woken** (A1–A8)
+- **Signal 1, 0 s:** the subagent's `idle_notification` arrives in the orchestrator transcript, and its `result` says what it is waiting on, e.g. "Waiting on the full-suite run to finish." (MAIN L62288).
+- **Signal 2, seconds later:** a `queue-operation` `enqueue` with a `<task-notification>` for a task id that appears in that subagent's transcript as "Command running in background with ID: X" (A1: enqueued at 18:03:52, 7 s after the idle notice). In A1, A3 and A7 the notice arrived within 2–6 min of the idle notice, and in A4–A6 and A8 within 5–12 min.
+- **Rule that catches every case:** if a subagent is idle and a task it owns completes, wake it at once. A weaker backstop: an idle subagent with a "waiting" result and no new commit or transcript line for 10 minutes.
+- **Recovery that worked:** a SendMessage telling the subagent to "read the output file now" (A1 L62392: PR done 4.5 min later; A8 L1440; A7 L20286). Prevention also worked: telling the builder to block on the run or poll its output itself (A9 L39639; GARMAN L21561, L22025). There were no stalls after those instructions.
+- **Note:** the harness's own tool result tells the subagent "You will be notified when it completes — do not poll that file or sleep" (e.g. cleanup-builder L638). For a subagent that is false, and it is what makes the subagent end its turn.
+
+**B. stdin hang** (B1, B2)
+- **Signal, about 60 s:** no Codex rollout appears under `~/.codex/sessions/<date>/` for that cwd after launch, and the task output file stays at 0 bytes (`bgj2gjmkj.output` was still 0 bytes after 2 h 21 min). Codex prints "Reading additional input from stdin…" before it creates a session, so nothing else records it.
+- **Recovery that worked:** kill, then relaunch with `</dev/null` (MAIN L71744; AIRFLO-B L3148).
+
+**C. Close-test hang** (C1, C2)
+- **Signal, about 8 min** (2× the normal 2.5–4 min run): pytest alive at 0.0 % CPU with the output file not growing (GARMAN L9436; `sample` shows `__psynch_cvwait`, L9466).
+- **Recovery that worked:** kill, run `./verify.sh` directly with stdout to a file and stdin from `/dev/null`, then close (GARMAN L9613). **Cause unknown.** It happens only under `review.mjs --close`.
+
+**D. Detached launch** (D1)
+- **Signal, 0 s:** the job's completion line in RLOG (`review-log.jsonl` L1386–1389 at 18:41–18:44), or the `exit N` line the detached job appends to its own log.
+- **Recovery:** launch with `run_in_background` or a Monitor on the exit marker, so completion becomes a notification. MAIN switched to this after H1: "restarting it as a tracked background job", GARMAN L1426.
+
+**E. Machine sleep** (E1–E5)
+- **Signal, before the stall:** in-flight jobs with no keep-awake assertion. During it: PMSET "Entering Sleep state due to 'Idle Sleep'" or "'Clamshell Sleep'", and "API Error: Your computer went to sleep mid-response" in Claude transcripts.
+- E2 slept **38 s** after the orchestrator launched a review and ended its turn.
+- **Recovery:** keep the Mac awake while any delegated job runs, e.g. `caffeinate -i` tied to the job. On battery with the lid closed that does not hold, which is what GARMAN reported at L21912. There, plug in or open the lid.
+
+**F. Unsent pane message** (F1)
+- **Signal, about 10 s:** after a send, the Codex rollout shows no new user turn or `task_started` (the rollout went silent from L332 at 01:21:53 to 01:27:56), and the pane screen shows "[Pasted Content N chars]" still in the input box (MAIN L84954).
+- **Recovery that worked:** submit again, then confirm the turn started (MAIN L84957).
+
+**G. Permission prompt** (G1)
+- **Signal, about 30 s:** the worker transcript ends on a `tool_use` with no `tool_result` (ac8f3f98 L51), and the pane shows a prompt.
+- **Recovery:** start pane workers in a mode that doesn't prompt (MAIN L84117).
+
+**H. Crashes:** already caught by the "failed" task notification within seconds. The gap is H3: the security pass can be missing while the wrapper still exits 0.
+
+## 3. Stall rate by launch method (Nov 7–14)
+
+| Launch method | Volume | Stalls (non-sleep) | Rate | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Native Claude subagent** (Agent tool, in-process teammate) | 119 spawns across 6 orchestrators; ~96 background-job completions owned by subagents | 8 incidents in 7 distinct subagents (all cause A) | **~6 % of spawns; ~8 % of subagent background jobs** | The only stall source with hours-long losses. All were Opus builders. |
+| **`codex exec`** (builders, Sol reviewers, test checks, QA) | ~697 rollouts | 2 stdin hangs (B) + 1 launch crash (H2) | **~0.4 %** | ~10 more rollouts stretched by sleep; 1 never completed (E3). |
+| **Interactive Codex in a cmux pane** | 20 codex-tui rollouts, nearly all Nov 14 experiments; 1 real build | 1 (F1) | 1 of 1 real build | Too few runs for a rate. |
+| **Interactive Claude in a pane** (experiment) | ~12 test sessions | 1 (G1) | n/a | Experiment only. |
+| **`claude -p`** (review.mjs reviewers, ask-model, QA `--chrome`, graders) | 1,925 sessions | **0 hangs found** (largest non-sleep gap: 10 min of active work) | ~0 % | ~20 `cmux: argument too large` failures happen before the session starts, so they aren't in the 1,925. |
+| **`review.mjs` wrapper** (both vendors) | 590 reviews + 383 closes | 2 close-test hangs (C) | ~0.5 % of closes | All 9 reviews over 25 min ran during machine sleep. |
+| **Detached shell job** `( … ) &` | ~120 launches (35 MAIN, 80 GARMAN, 5 other; pattern match, approximate) | 1 confirmed (D1); C2 also detached | — | No completion signal by design. |
+
+## 4. What the orchestrator did that caused or hid stalls
+
+1. **It relayed "waiting" as "fine" without checking whether the thing awaited had already finished.**
+   - Examples: MAIN L62291 "waiting on its full test run … Nothing needs you" (the suite had finished 4 s earlier); GARMAN L12577, L12681, L17926 ("Nothing needs you right now" while dk-live had been idle for 12 h); CI L1376.
+   - In A1 it relayed the stale status twice before the user asked.
+2. **It dismissed repeated idle notices as "the builder repeating its report"** about 215 times (MAIN 83, GARMAN 78, CI 21, AIRFLO 24, PERSONAL 9). Each idle notice is the one built-in signal that an agent has stopped. Treating it as noise hid A2, A4, A6 and A7.
+3. **It told the user things were running when nobody had checked:**
+   - MAIN L62338: "nothing stopped"
+   - CI L1400: "being built now"
+   - AIRFLO-B L3001: "the reviewer is partway through reading the diff" (it was hung on stdin)
+   - MAIN L84933: "you can watch it work on them" (the message was never submitted)
+4. **Unverified sends.** F1's paste was never confirmed as received. The pane waiter (`bg9nijlqi`) only watched for DONE, so "idle with unsent input" looked the same as "working".
+5. **Untracked launches.** About 120 `( … ) & echo started` jobs, mostly in GARMAN, give no completion notice. D1 lost about an hour this way.
+6. **The `codex exec` stdin mistake recurred after it was flagged.** It was flagged on Nov 11 (B1, field report bf01bc) and recurred in another session on Nov 13 (B2). About 18 `codex exec` calls in background shells had no `</dev/null` (pattern match).
+7. **After a prod it woke only one of two idle builders.** On Nov 13 at 19:22 it woke dk-live-builder but not fc-pr3-builder, which stayed idle 4 h 49 min longer (A7).
+8. **It used fixed `sleep` watchdogs** (MAIN `sleep 1800` / `sleep 2400`, Nov 9, after A1), which can only fire long after a stall. Later it moved to event waiters (task notifications, Monitors).
+9. **Nothing keeps the Mac awake.** The orchestrator launched long jobs and ended its turn, and the Mac idle-slept 38 s later (E2). GARMAN noticed only on Nov 14 (L21912).
+10. **The record of work only logs successes.** `review-log.jsonl` writes a line when a review finishes, not when it starts, so a hung or killed review (E3, C1, C2) leaves no trace there.
+
+## 5. What I could not verify
+
+- **Why pytest hangs only under `review.mjs --close`** (C1, C2). I have the symptom (0 % CPU, `__psynch_cvwait`) but not the cause.
+- **The model behind the B1 QA lane.** It used the `codex` shell function's default; I didn't resolve which model that is.
+- **D1's exact loss.** The Ledgerline fix checks and the Docket review finished by 18:44 (RLOG). I couldn't time when the detached Sol test check and the Codex QA re-test finished, because their logs aren't in the task folder.
+- **A2's real cost**, given the orchestrator was also waiting on the user over the same span.
+- **The harness mechanism.** I infer that a subagent's task notice goes to the parent queue and is never delivered, from the parent-queue enqueue/remove entries plus the subagent transcript showing nothing until the next team-lead message. I did not read harness code.
+- **The cmux event log** (`~/.cmuxterm/events.jsonl`). I didn't check it for F1 or G1. It exists and records agent hook events, so it may give an earlier signal than the ones above.
+- **Whether the user was present during the sleep windows.** Idle Sleep implies no input, but I can't say whether he was waiting.
+- **Before Nov 8 01:43 UTC** the power log has no entries, so the 15-min gaps in cleanup-builder on Nov 7 00:07–01:22 UTC (also outside the 7-day window) are unexplained.
+- **Other sessions** (FairDivide, ortegasolutions, 2eef288d, mercor) were checked by keyword for prods only. None turned up a delegated-agent stall in the window.
+- **Approximate counts.** The "repeat report" dismissals, detached launches and missing `</dev/null` are regex counts.
diff --git a/lib/agent.js b/lib/agent.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a8b7976
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/agent.js
@@ -0,0 +1,523 @@
+import fs from 'node:fs';
+import path from 'node:path';
+import crypto from 'node:crypto';
+import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';
+import { readUserText } from './paths.js';
+import { homeDir, resolveModel, vendorOf, EFFORTS } from './models.js';
+import { ROLE_RE } from './roles.js';
+
+const sleep = ms => new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
+const quote = s => `'${String(s).replace(/'/g, `'\\''`)}'`;
+const bad = message => Object.assign(new Error(message), { exitCode: 2 });
+const dir = () => path.join(homeDir(), '.agent-config-studio', 'agents');
+const eventFile = () => path.join(homeDir(), '.cmuxterm', 'events.jsonl');
+function text(file) {
+  try { return readUserText(file); } catch (e) { if (e.code === 'ENOENT') return ''; throw e; }
+}
+function lines(file) {
+  return text(file).split('\n').flatMap(line => { try { return [JSON.parse(line)]; } catch { return []; } });
+}
+function children(folder) {
+  try { return fs.readdirSync(folder, { withFileTypes: true }); } catch (e) { if (e.code === 'ENOENT') return []; throw e; }
+}
+function atomic(file, body, mode = 0o600) {
+  fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(file), { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });
+  const tmp = `${file}.tmp-${crypto.randomUUID()}`;
+  try { fs.writeFileSync(tmp, body, { flag: 'wx', mode }); fs.renameSync(tmp, file); }
+  finally { fs.rmSync(tmp, { force: true }); }
+}
+function save(w) { atomic(path.join(dir(), `${w.id}.json`), JSON.stringify(w, null, 2) + '\n'); }
+function decodeSession(value, vendor) {
+  if (typeof value !== 'string' || !value) return null;
+  if (!value.startsWith('cmux-feed-v1:')) return value;
+  const parts = value.split(':');
+  if (parts.length !== 3) return null;
+  const decoded = parts.slice(1).map(part => {
+    if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9+/]+={0,2}$/.test(part)) return null;
+    const bytes = Buffer.from(part, 'base64');
+    return bytes.toString('base64').replace(/=+$/, '') === part.replace(/=+$/, '') ? bytes.toString('utf8') : null;
+  });
+  return decoded[0] === vendor && decoded[1] && !/[\0\ufffd]/.test(decoded[1]) ? decoded[1] : null;
+}
+function normalizeWorker(w) { w.session = decodeSession(w.session, w.vendor); return w; }
+function all() { return children(dir()).filter(d => d.isFile() && d.name.endsWith('.json')).map(d => normalizeWorker(JSON.parse(readUserText(path.join(dir(), d.name))))); }
+function cmuxError(message) { return Object.assign(new Error(`cmux: ${message}`), { cmuxCode: /\bnot_found\b/.test(message) ? 'not_found' : null }); }
+function cmux(args) {
+  const r = spawnSync('cmux', ['--json', '--id-format', 'both', ...args], { encoding: 'utf8', env: { ...process.env, CMUX_QUIET: '1' }, stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'], timeout: 10000, maxBuffer: 8 * 1024 * 1024 });
+  if (r.error || r.status !== 0) throw cmuxError(r.error?.message || r.stderr.trim() || r.stdout.trim());
+  let result;
+  try { result = JSON.parse(r.stdout); } catch {
+    if (args[0] === 'read-screen') return r.stdout;
+    throw new Error('cmux returned invalid JSON');
+  }
+  if (result.ok === false || result.error) throw cmuxError(JSON.stringify(result.error || result));
+  return result.result || result;
+}
+function ref(value, type) {
+  if (typeof value !== 'string' || (!value.startsWith(`${type}:`) && !/^[a-f\d-]{36}$/i.test(value))) throw new Error(`cmux did not return a ${type} ref`);
+  return value;
+}
+export function context() {
+  if (!process.env.CMUX_SOCKET_PATH) throw bad('agent needs cmux: run it inside a cmux terminal');
+  let identity;
+  try { identity = cmux(['identify']); } catch { throw bad('agent needs cmux: its socket is unreachable'); }
+  const caller = identity.caller || {};
+  const workspace = process.env.CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID || caller.workspace_ref || identity.workspace_ref;
+  let pane = caller.pane_ref;
+  if (!pane && process.env.CMUX_SURFACE_ID) {
+    const out = cmux(['identify', '--workspace', ref(workspace, 'workspace'), '--surface', process.env.CMUX_SURFACE_ID]);
+    pane = out.caller?.pane_ref || out.surface?.pane_ref || out.pane_ref;
+
+  }
+  return { workspace: ref(workspace, 'workspace'), pane: ref(pane, 'pane') };
+}
+function owned(w, ctx) { return w.workspace === ctx.workspace && w.orchestratorPane === ctx.pane; }
+export function worker(id, ctx) {
+  if (!/^[a-f\d-]{36}$/i.test(id || '')) throw bad('invalid worker id');
+  const w = normalizeWorker(JSON.parse(readUserText(path.join(dir(), `${id}.json`))));
+  if (!owned(w, ctx)) throw bad('worker belongs to another orchestrator');
+  return w;
+}
+function candidates(w) {
+  const home = homeDir();
+  if (w.vendor === 'codex') {
+    const root = path.join(home, '.codex', 'sessions');
+    let dirs = [root];
+    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) dirs = dirs.flatMap(d => children(d).filter(e => e.isDirectory()).map(e => path.join(d, e.name)));
+    return dirs.flatMap(d => children(d).filter(e => e.isFile() && /^rollout-.*\.jsonl$/.test(e.name)).map(e => path.join(d, e.name)));
+  }
+  if (w.vendor === 'claude') {
+    const root = path.join(home, '.claude', 'projects');
+    return children(root).filter(e => e.isDirectory()).flatMap(d => children(path.join(root, d.name)).filter(e => e.isFile() && e.name.endsWith('.jsonl') && (!w.session || e.name === `${w.session}.jsonl`)).map(e => path.join(root, d.name, e.name)));
+  }
+  const root = path.join(home, '.grok', 'sessions', w.cwd.replace(/\//g, '%2F'));
+  return children(root).filter(e => e.isDirectory()).map(e => path.join(root, e.name, 'events.jsonl'));
+}
+function hooks(w) {
+  return [...new Map(lines(eventFile()).slice(w.eventStart).filter(e => String(e.surface_id || '').toLowerCase() === String(w.surface_id).toLowerCase()).map(e => [JSON.stringify(e), e])).values()];
+}
+function discover(w, events, at = Date.now()) {
+  normalizeWorker(w);
+  const session = e => decodeSession(e.session_id, w.vendor) || decodeSession(e.payload?.session_id, w.vendor);
+  const start = events.find(e => e.name === 'agent.hook.SessionStart' && session(e) && (!w.session || session(e) === w.session));
+  w.session ||= start ? session(start) : null;
+  if (w.session && w.sessionStartedAt == null) {
+    const stamp = Date.parse(start?.occurred_at || start?.timestamp || start?.ts || '');
+    w.sessionStartedAt = Number.isFinite(stamp) ? stamp : at;
+  }
+  if (w.transcript) return;
+  const peers = all().filter(r => r.id !== w.id);
+  const claimed = new Set(peers.map(r => r.transcript).filter(Boolean));
+  if (!w.session && peers.some(r => r.vendor === w.vendor && r.cwd === w.cwd && !r.session && r.status !== 'closed')) return;
+  const matches = candidates(w).filter(f => {
+    if (claimed.has(f) || w.baseline.includes(f)) return false;
+    if (w.vendor === 'codex') {
+      const meta = lines(f)[0]?.payload;
+      return meta?.cwd === w.cwd && (!w.session || decodeSession(meta.id, w.vendor) === w.session);
+    }
+    if (w.vendor === 'claude' && !w.session) return lines(f).some(e => e.cwd === w.cwd);
+    const id = w.vendor === 'grok' ? path.basename(path.dirname(f)) : path.basename(f, '.jsonl');
+    return !w.session || id === w.session;
+  });
+  // An ambiguous cwd is not proof of ownership. Wait for the surface's SessionStart.
+  if (matches.length !== 1) return;
+  w.transcript = matches[0];
+  w.session ||= decodeSession(w.vendor === 'codex' ? lines(w.transcript)[0]?.payload?.id : w.vendor === 'grok' ? path.basename(path.dirname(w.transcript)) : path.basename(w.transcript, '.jsonl'), w.vendor);
+  if (w.session) w.sessionStartedAt ??= at;
+}
+function lastSteps(entries) {
+  const steps = [];
+  for (const e of entries) {
+    const blocks = e.message?.content ?? e.content;
+    const items = Array.isArray(blocks) ? blocks : [e.payload || e];
+    for (const item of items) {
+      if (!['function_call', 'custom_tool_call', 'tool_use', 'tool_call', 'tool_started', 'command'].includes(item.type || item.kind)) continue;
+      let input = item.arguments ?? item.input ?? item.command ?? item.data ?? item.content ?? '';
+      if (typeof input === 'string') { try { input = JSON.parse(input); } catch {} }
+      const detail = typeof input === 'object' && input !== null ? input.cmd ?? input.command ?? JSON.stringify(input) : input;
+      steps.push(`${item.name || item.tool_name || item.type}: ${detail}`.slice(0, 2000));
+    }
+  }
+  return steps.slice(-3);
+}
+function toolCommand(item) {
+  let input = item.arguments ?? item.rawInput ?? item.input ?? item.command ?? item.data ?? item.content ?? '';
+  if (typeof input === 'string') { try { input = JSON.parse(input); } catch {} }
+  if (input && typeof input === 'object' && !Array.isArray(input)) input = input.cmd ?? input.command ?? JSON.stringify(input);
+  return Array.isArray(input) ? input.join(' ') : String(input || item.name || item.toolName || 'tool (input unavailable)');
+}
+function toolsIn(entries) {
+  const open = new Map();
+  let structured = false;
+  for (const [index, e] of entries.entries()) {
+    const body = e.message?.content ?? e.content;
+    const item = e.payload || e;
+    if (['task_started', 'task_complete', 'turn_started', 'turn_ended'].includes(item.type || e.event)
+      || (e.type === 'user' || e.role === 'user') && (typeof body === 'string' || Array.isArray(body) && body.some(b => b.type === 'text'))) { open.clear(); structured = false; }
+    const blocks = [...(Array.isArray(body) ? body : [item]), ...(e.tool_calls || []).map(t => ({ ...t, type: 'tool_call' }))];
+    for (const [block, t] of blocks.entries()) {
+      const type = t.type || t.kind;
+      const id = t.call_id ?? t.tool_use_id ?? t.tool_call_id ?? t.toolCallId ?? t.id;
+      const key = id ? `call:${id}` : `anonymous:${index}:${block}`;
+      if (['function_call_output', 'custom_tool_call_output', 'tool_result', 'exec_command_end', 'custom_tool_call_end', 'tool_completed'].includes(type)
+        || type === 'tool_call_update' && ['completed', 'failed', 'cancelled'].includes(t.status)) {
+        if (id) open.delete(key);
+        else {
+          const anonymous = [...open.keys()].find(k => k.startsWith('anonymous:'));
+          if (anonymous) open.delete(anonymous);
+        }
+      } else if (['function_call', 'custom_tool_call', 'tool_use', 'tool_call', 'exec_command_begin', 'custom_tool_call_begin', 'tool_started'].includes(type)) {
+        structured = true;
+        if (!open.has(key)) {
+          const stamp = e.timestamp ?? e.ts ?? e.occurred_at ?? t.timestamp;
+          const at = typeof stamp === 'number' ? stamp : Date.parse(stamp || '');
+          open.set(key, { key, command: toolCommand(t), at: Number.isFinite(at) ? at : null });
+        }
+      }
+    }
+    if (e.message?.stop_reason === 'end_turn' || e.stop_reason === 'end_turn') open.clear();
+  }
+  return { open: [...open.values()], structured };
+}
+export function snapshot(w, at = Date.now()) {
+  const events = hooks(w);
+  discover(w, events, at);
+  const transcript = w.transcript ? lines(w.transcript) : [];
+  const historyFile = w.vendor === 'grok' && w.transcript ? path.join(path.dirname(w.transcript), 'chat_history.jsonl') : null;
+  const history = historyFile ? lines(historyFile) : transcript;
+  const users = history.filter(e => {
+    if (w.vendor === 'codex') return e.type === 'event_msg' && e.payload?.type === 'user_message';
+    if (!(e.type === 'user' || e.role === 'user' || e.message?.role === 'user')) return false;
+    const content = e.message?.content ?? e.content;
+    return typeof content === 'string' || Array.isArray(content) && content.some(b => b.type === 'text');
