    {
      "issue": "Transcript discovery ignores alternate harness homes. ACS’s generated shell exports CODEX_HOME for private Codex seats, but discovery always searches ~/.codex. A completed worker therefore returns timeout with transcriptMissing, and answer fails. GROK_HOME has the same defect. Both cases reproduced using in-memory transcripts.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "84",
      "quote": "    const root = path.join(home, '.codex', 'sessions');",
      "suggestion": "Persist the effective harness home when launching each worker and use it for all subsequent transcript discovery.",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 7,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "Open a Codex worker using an ACS private account home, or a Grok worker with GROK_HOME configured, then run wait or answer.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 35,
      "severity": "medium",
      "filed": false,
      "instances": [
        {
          "file": "lib/agent.js",
          "line": "84",
          "quote": "    const root = path.join(home, '.codex', 'sessions');"
        },
        {
          "file": "lib/agent.js",
          "line": "93",
          "quote": "  const root = path.join(home, '.grok', 'sessions', w.cwd.replace(/\\//g, '%2F'));"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f1"
    },
    {
      "issue": "A follow-up typed directly into the worker pane remains classified as done because turnComplete advances only through agent send. Reproduction returned done while the new turn had an open tool, then force-closed the active worker after 30 minutes. This also excludes active work from the four-worker limit and disables its stall checks.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "312",
      "quote": "  if (!pending && s.complete > w.turnComplete) signals.push({ state: 'done', at: w.finishedAt });",
      "suggestion": "Track the latest started and completed turns from transcript ordering, including turns submitted directly in the pane, and update activity accordingly.",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 7,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "After a worker finishes, type and submit a correction directly in its cmux pane, then invoke wait or list.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 21,
      "severity": "medium",
      "filed": false,
      "instances": [
        {
          "file": "lib/agent.js",
          "line": "312",
          "quote": "  if (!pending && s.complete > w.turnComplete) signals.push({ state: 'done', at: w.finishedAt });"
        },
        {
          "file": "lib/agent.js",
          "line": "277",
          "quote": "  const runningTurn = s.started > (w.turnStarted || 0) && s.complete <= w.turnComplete;"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f2"
    },
    {
      "issue": "Resolved permission requests remain stuck until the entire turn completes. The historical PermissionRequest remains selected even after its matching tool result appears. Reproduction still returned stuck while a subsequent command exceeded command-after, so the obsolete permission event masks later faults.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "274",
      "quote": "  const stuck = fresh.find(e => e.name === 'agent.hook.PermissionRequest' || (e.name === 'agent.hook.Notification' && (!w.finishedAt || Math.abs(Date.parse(e.occurred_at || '') - w.finishedAt) > 65000 || !e.occurred_at)));\n  const blocked = stuck && (s.complete <= w.turnComplete || Date.parse(stuck.occurred_at || '') > w.finishedAt);",
      "suggestion": "Retire permission events when subsequent transcript activity proves resolution, and verify that the dialog remains active before returning stuck.",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 7,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "Approve a worker’s permission dialog in its pane, then wait again while the same turn continues executing tools.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 21,
      "severity": "medium",
      "filed": false,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f3"
    },
    {
      "issue": "Prompt files can inject harness options and execute attacker-supplied MCP commands. The launcher passes prompt contents without an end-of-options delimiter. An attacker-controlled brief beginning with `--config=mcp_servers.evil={command=\"sh\",args=[\"-c\",\"<command>\"]}` therefore configures a process instead of becoming task text. This exposes the operator's account to command execution outside the worker's workspace sandbox. A harmless parser probe confirmed that this argument creates an enabled stdio MCP server.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "392",
      "quote": "    atomic(w.launcher, `#!/bin/sh\\ncd ${quote(cwd)} || exit 1\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' \"$$\" > ${quote(w.pidFile)}\\ncaffeinate -i -w \"$$\" </dev/null > ${quote(path.join(w.runDir, 'caffeinate.log'))} 2>&1 &\\nset -- ${args.map(quote).join(' ')}\\n${gitAccess}exec ${testMode && process.env.AGENT_TEST_BINARY ? quote(binary) : vendor} \"$@\" \"$(cat ${quote(w.promptFile)})\"\\n`, 0o700);",
      "suggestion": "Insert the harness-supported end-of-options delimiter before prompt contents, and test that option-shaped prompts remain literal task text.",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 10,
      "protected": true,
      "trigger": "Run `agent open sol --prompt-file task.md` in a trusted workspace where an attacker supplied task.md containing an MCP configuration option.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 30,
      "severity": "high",
      "filed": false,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "source": "security",
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "issue": "Sending a follow-up can approve a trust or permission dialog without the operator's consent. sendWorker refreshes the worker but proceeds even when its state is stuck; sendTurn then presses Enter up to four times. At an affirmative dialog selection, those keys authorize the pending action instead of submitting a message. An attacker-induced permission request can consequently execute against the operator's files when the orchestrator sends a correction. In-memory execution confirmed that both trust-stuck and permission-stuck workers receive Enter.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "487",
      "quote": "    cmux(['send-key', '--workspace', w.workspace, '--surface', w.surface_ref, 'enter']);",
      "suggestion": "Reject sends while trust or permission approval is pending. Recheck for dialogs before Enter retries and stop without answering when one appears.",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 9,
      "protected": true,
      "trigger": "A worker encounters a trust dialog or requests permission for an attacker-induced command; the orchestrator calls `agent send <id> \"Do not approve anything\"` while the affirmative choice is selected.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 27,
      "severity": "high",
      "filed": false,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "source": "security",
      "id": "s2"
    }
  ],
